<!--
SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 Sythos (https://www.sythos.net)
Author: Sythos (https://www.sythos.net)

Plesk extension descriptor template. build-plesk-package.ts substitutes the
version placeholder in the <version> tag below with the version from
package.json and writes the result to the root of the generated ZIP archive
(Plesk requires meta.xml at the archive root - see
packaging/plesk/build-plesk-package.ts).

plesk_min_version: this project's Plesk adapter (src/platform/plesk/) talks
to the modern REST API v2 (`/api/v2/*`), which shipped with the Plesk
Obsidian line. 18.0.29 is used here as a conservative floor based on the
prior research referenced by this task (Plesk Obsidian's first widely
available release carrying REST API v2); this has NOT been verified against
a real Plesk instance and should be confirmed (or tightened/loosened) before
a production release - see src/platform/plesk/README.md for the same caveat
already documented for the REST endpoints this package's adapter calls.
plesk_max_version is left open-ended (any 18.x) rather than pinned, since
nothing in this extension depends on a specific Obsidian patch release.
-->
<meta>
    <id>gulogulo</id>
    <name>Gulo Gulo</name>
    <description>Gulo Gulo groupware runtime (mail, calendar, contacts) running as a dedicated systemd service behind this domain's reverse proxy.</description>
    <version>@VERSION@</version>
    <release>1</release>
    <vendor>Sythos (https://www.sythos.net)</vendor>
    <url>https://github.com/Sythos/GuloGulo</url>
    <plesk_min_version>18.0.29</plesk_min_version>
    <plesk_max_version>18.999.999</plesk_max_version>
    <os>unix</os>
</meta>
